TY  - JOUR
T1  - Review ofImproving memory through creativity: A professional's guide to culturally sensitive cognitive training with older adults
AN  - 1674701259; 2015-13527-008
AB  - Reviews the book, 
Improving Memory Through Creativity: A Professional’s Guide to Culturally Sensitive Cognitive Training With Older Adults by Amanda Alders Pike (2013). Pike builds upon the success of cognitive training as a technique for delaying cognitive and functional decline in older adults. Although cognitive training usually consists of memory drills and verbal exercises, Pike argues that creative self-expression is perfectly suited for cognitive training as art creates a hospitable environment for memory improvement in the brain. She further argues that creativity-based cognitive training is inherently culturally sensitive as it bypasses verbal communication. New clinicians will benefit from the practical guidance for creating sessions, and seasoned professionals will find insight into why their interventions are effective and how to improve upon them. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2025 APA, all rights reserved)
