TY  - JOUR
T1  - Effets généraux et difféerentiels d'un programe d'entraînement cognitif multimodal chez la personne âgée
TT  - General and differential effects of a multimodal cognitive training program for the elderly
AN  - 619686418; 2001-17208-003
AB  - Examined the efficiency of a cognitive training program on 80-yr-old Ss" performance measures on 8 cognitive tasks (attentional control, memory, and reasoning). 64 Ss in the experimental group attended 6 multimodal cognitive training sessions in the 3 task group areas, while 18 control Ss took part in 6 discussion sessions. Ss" cognitive performances before and just after the program, as well as 6 and 9 mo later, were compared. Results show a significant gain in cognitive performance on memory tasks even several months after the training program. The individual differences analysis shows that the training program was primarily effective for Ss characterized by high levels of performance on preliminary cognitive tests. Two conclusions are advanced: (1) cognitive plasticity may not be possible for very aged people with low cognitive levels and limited educational background, and (2) that cognitive programs should be adapted with regard to less abstract exercises based on participants" cognitive levels. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2022 APA, all rights reserved)
